# Citroen CX Series 1 four-door saloon, 1975-1985.
#
# The first-generation CX, launched on 26 August 1974 and sold in right-hand
# drive in Britain from 1975. The Series 2 replaced it in July 1985.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citro%C3%ABn_CX (cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.666 x 1.730 x 1.360 m, wheelbase 2.845 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes. The hull measures 4.666 m on a 2.845 m wheelbase (61.0 per
# cent) and 1.730 m wide.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation, used directly; image
# 2 the front three-quarter and image 3 the rear, showing the concave rear
# screen and the partly covered rear wheels. The model was built as the low
# aerodynamic wedge with the narrow glasshouse, the long wheelbase and the rear
# spats, and sits low on its suspension as the photographed car does.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found, so the objects carry plain
# names: silver, blue, grey and red. Weights silver 3, blue 3, grey 2, red 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase. Chrome keeps its own
# material.
#
# Speed 190 km/h, the 2.5-litre injection car's quoted maximum. Comfort
# 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90: the hydropneumatic suspension and the
# long wheelbase made it one of the most comfortable cars of its class.
# Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1975 intro, retires staggered 1995-1998 on a twenty-
# to twenty-three-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/citroen-cx-series1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/citroen-cx-series1.dae (67 objects). References:
# citycars/references/citroen-cx-series1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is more slab-like than the photographs and the
# rear overhang is longer than the real car's, so the tail reads as a fastback
# rather than the CX's short, cut-off rear. At 128 px the low wedge, the covered
# rear wheels and the concave rear screen read as a Series 1 CX.

obj=citycar
name=CitroenCXSeries1(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1975
intro_month=5
retire_year=1998
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=465

